From d61188828288645a8da79832c8e44c862faf9418 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: astrangedaytoday15-dev <342675337+astrangedaytoday15-dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 03:03:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] World 3D S3: viewer tile set and follow window

- InstanceSceneView.render takes one scene URL or several drawn together
  (World 3D's tiles); unload() frees a scene's geometry, materials and
  textures, and a load still in flight when unloaded is dropped.
- renderer/scripts/utils/world-window.ts: the N x N tile window round one
  followed unit, nearest tile first; follows past a 40-yard hysteresis,
  keeps the last N tiles left behind, drops everything on a map change;
  worldTilesToLoad asks for at most two tiles at once.
- Each building and prop is drawn by one tile only: export-tile.mjs's
  placementOwner picks, by uniqueId, the tile under its origin when that
  tile lists it, otherwise the first listing tile round it;
  exportMapScene takes keepPlacement. Tile schema and cache version 2.
- Tests for ownership, the window, and load pacing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
